From c775e21ce33457d09cbbb3aeb768f8720e8e69da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liew Rui Yan <aethernet65535@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:43:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon: fix quota could not be set to zero

When the temporal quota goal tuner determines that the goal has been
achieved (score >= 10000), it sets esz_bp to zero so that the effective
quota becomes error.  However, damos_set_effective_quota()
unconditionally clamps the quota to min_region_sz, preventing the quota
from ever reaching zero.

Skip the min_region_sz clamping when esz is already zero so that the
temporal tuner's intent is respected.

Signed-off-by: Liew Rui Yan <aethernet65535@gmail.com>
---
 mm/damon/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index 644daf5a1656..6f141a092cd9 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -3112,7 +3112,8 @@ static void damos_set_effective_quota(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damos *s)
 		else
 			throughput = PAGE_SIZE * 1024;
 		esz = min(throughput * quota->ms, esz);
-		esz = max(ctx->min_region_sz, esz);
+		if (esz)
+			esz = max(ctx->min_region_sz, esz);
 	}
 
 	if (quota->sz && quota->sz < esz)
-- 
